    "Open Design Specification for .dwg files v5.4.1 section 20.4.104",
    "https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2027/ENU/OARX-RefGuide/files/OARX-RefGuide-DXF_Group_Codes.html"
  ],
  "change": "Decode the existing XRECORD Int16 group ranges as signed two-byte values. Extend the bounded legacy XRECORD source observer to compare signed values against their exact 16-bit wire representation. The public typed value now exposes the signed result.",
  "checks": [
    "A generated frame tests values -32768, -123, -1, 0 and 32767 across 13 representative Int16 group codes in R13/R14 and generated R2004/R2007 controls. R13/R14 truncation resets and corrected retries pass; group-70 source proof binds signed values to the raw bits.",
    "Nine focused normal-build XRECORD, compatibility, codepage, source and legacy CTests pass; the legacy test also passes AddressSanitizer on macOS ARM64 with leak detection unavailable.",
    "An independent LibreDWG wire observer verifies class, identities, payload boundary, handle roles and corrupted-length refusal/retry for both producer-reopened files.",
    "A scratch-only guard-bypassed diagnostic tests both ASCII and binary outputs for each source; an injected staged XRECORD mismatch preserves the destination and permits same-adapter retry. Physical tags and ezdxf independently read -123 and the selected owner graph with zero audit errors or fixes.",
    "The unmodified production policy refuses both source files atomically in both encodings; default generator and observer values still pass."
  ],
  "finding": "XRECORD integer groups except 370-379 were decoded as unsigned. In two generated source files the producer and LibreDWG independently read group 70 bytes 0xff85 as -123, while the prior libdxfrw reader reported 65413.",
  "id": "p6-legacy-xrecord-signed-int16-2026-11-28",
  "limitations": [
    "The R13/R14 drawings are generated locally with acadrust, not independent native AutoCAD producers.",
    "Scratch-only guard bypass is not production output qualification; native dictionary cloning and complete whole-file semantics remain open.",
    "Generated R2004/R2007 parser vectors prove decoding only, not independent producer qualification for those versions."
  ],
